    "title": "Rat in a Maze",
    "category": "Recursion",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given an N \u00d7 N binary matrix where 1 represents an open cell and 0 represents a blocked cell, find all possible paths from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner. The rat may move only Up, Down, Left, and Right, and cannot visit the same cell more than once in a path. Print all valid paths in lexicographical order.",
    "input": "Integer N Matrix maze",
    "output": "All valid paths.",
    "constraints": "1 <= N <= 10"
